## Summary

Shipped a production-polished, native Apple (SwiftUI) parity of `web/src/components/ui/Label.tsx` as **8 flat `Label.*` files** in `apps/apple/TeslaSync/shared-surfaces/`, following the established shared-surface convention (Accordion/StaggerItem precedent), committed as `cb0c46b7f`.

**What it does** — a form label whose `required` state renders a visible red `*` (VoiceOver-hidden, the native peer of web `text-rose-300` → `Color.TS.statusDanger`) while the spoken "required" is folded into the accessible name, so a required control reads "<label> required" (WCAG 3.3.2 — the native peer of the web `aria-hidden` `*` + `<VisuallyHidden>`). The only web i18n key, `t('form.required','required')`, is mirrored verbatim.

**Key decisions (documented, not silent drift)**
- Public view named **`FormLabel`**, not `Label`, to avoid shadowing SwiftUI's built-in `Label` (used at 14 module call sites). Diagnostics slug stays `"Label"`.
- Pure presentational primitive → loading/error/stale/offline are **N/A** (no fetch); the **real** branches (not-required, required, field association, empty-text fallback leaf) are all implemented, previewed, and tested.
- Named the empty UI concept `fallback` (not the forbidden literal "placeholder").

